WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.784
This slide shows four columns that could all be
stored as integers Heart rate

00:00:05.798 --> 00:00:12.155
is a measurement recorded to whole units Emergency
visits is a count Patient

00:00:12.182 --> 00:00:17.936
ID is a label Satisfaction is ordinal The

00:00:17.963 --> 00:00:23.626
same technical dtype supports four different
analytical meanings This is why

00:00:23.639 --> 00:00:29.416
the correct question is not what dtype does pandas
show The correct question

00:00:29.443 --> 00:00:33.443
is how was this value generated and what comparisons
make sense
